WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.150
Let's get right into it.

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:05.341
Normally, I would waste a ton of time at the
top of the show talking about the show, but

00:00:05.341 --> 00:00:07.420
we actually have too much show today.

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:09.980
So let's just get right into it.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:18.740
I'm a little worried that there are too many
people on the left who are not seriously looking

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:25.580
at Joe Biden's proposals and platform, particularly
his economic proposals, not looking at them

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:31.699
seriously enough and giving credit where credit
is due for what?

00:00:31.699 --> 00:00:38.580
Guess would be the most progressive economic
platform of an American president in decades

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.580
and decades.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:44.760
And I would argue even going beyond the high
marginal tax rates of Eisenhower's administration.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.629
I'll explain why and a little bit.

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:51.210
There's a very good piece in MarketWatch called
Liberals aren't giving Joe Biden credit for

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:54.559
a radical tax plan that goes after the indolent
rich.

00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:56.059
The article is by Nick Buffi.

00:00:56.059 --> 00:00:57.329
We're linking to it on YouTube.

00:00:57.329 --> 00:00:59.200
I encourage you to read it.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:04.239
And the article accurately points out, as
I've been pointing out for months, that there

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:09.539
is a contingent of the left that is branding
Joe Biden as sort of like the ultimate centrist,

00:01:09.539 --> 00:01:18.299
the epitome of the Democratic candidate who
is almost a Republican or would have been

00:01:18.299 --> 00:01:20.469
a Republican in times past.

00:01:20.469 --> 00:01:23.020
I think that that could not be further from
the truth.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:28.060
Now, I've said this phrase, it would be the
most progressive economic platform in modern

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:29.090
political history.

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:33.950
And there were people writing me saying, David,
it's meaningless because it's 2020.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:35.049
What's how is that meaningless?

00:01:35.049 --> 00:01:36.070
It's accurate.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:37.070
Okay.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:40.789
You can say times have changed and our expectations
have moved to the left, and that's a good

00:01:40.789 --> 00:01:41.789
thing.

00:01:41.789 --> 00:01:47.079
And therefore, it is also a good thing if
our elected officials are following the movement

00:01:47.079 --> 00:01:49.319
of the country politically.

00:01:49.319 --> 00:01:53.520
And the concern for me is coming partially
from I think that there are some on the left

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.989
who are just ideologically blinded.

00:01:55.989 --> 00:01:58.630
And then there are others who just aren't
looking at the proposals.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:03.200
So let's focus in on the tax proposals that
Joe Biden has.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.259
Separate yourself from ideology.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:12.870
And separate yourself from what would be the
perfect and analyze what is Joe Biden's platform?

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:19.739
Joe Biden would raise the corporate profit
tax and establish what is effectively a minimum

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:26.489
tax for corporations similar to the alternative
minimum tax that people have had since individuals

00:02:26.489 --> 00:02:28.900
have had since 1969.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:37.129
That is radical in a context where both parties
have allowed these zero tax dollar status

00:02:37.129 --> 00:02:40.709
quo of corporations to perpetuate itself.

00:02:40.709 --> 00:02:45.390
Joe Biden would eliminate deductions for high
income earners.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:52.760
Joe Biden would repeal most of the Trump tax
cuts and increase taxes on fossil fuel emissions.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:58.790
So Joe Biden would uncap starting at four
hundred thousand dollars.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:03.080
The 12 percent tax for Social Security.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:05.329
That is absolutely massive.

00:03:05.329 --> 00:03:12.810
I actually don't think for a moment I'm going
to imagine it's not that people don't care,

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:15.810
it's that people don't understand the magnitude
of that.

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:22.829
You would see a CEO who earns ten million
dollars a year go from paying a zero point

00:03:22.829 --> 00:03:29.659
two percent effective Social Security tax
to a 12 percent effective Social Security

00:03:29.659 --> 00:03:30.909
tax.

00:03:30.909 --> 00:03:36.650
That is a massively radical proposal, which
you will see all sorts of people fight tooth

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:40.040
and nail to prevent from becoming a reality.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:44.709
And then Joe Biden would take those revenues
and reinvest them in raising Social Security

00:03:44.709 --> 00:03:46.409
benefits for the poor.

00:03:46.409 --> 00:03:52.040
That's exactly the type of policy that a Bernie
Sanders type would put in place.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:56.420
There are hundreds of thousands of seniors
who would be immediately pulled out of poverty

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:01.709
as a result of that policy without it costing
the middle class a penny.

00:04:01.709 --> 00:04:02.709
Some say a dime.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:04.400
I say a penny.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:10.549
As we know, capital gains is something that
allows the super rich who don't work to pay

00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:16.810
less as an effective tax rate than many people
who do work capital gains, long term capital

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:22.190
gains taxed at a far lower rate than earned
income for the rich.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:28.740
Joe Biden has proposed eliminating that lower
capital gains rate on dividends and long term

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:33.080
capital gains for everybody making above a
million dollars per year.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:38.669
If you combine that with raising the top tax
rate back to close to 40 percent, that is

00:04:38.669 --> 00:04:44.490
a combination of proposals from Joe Biden,
which would nearly double the average tax

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:46.860
rate for non working millionaires.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:52.190
The Tax Policy Center has analyzed this proposal
and has found that three quarters of Joe Biden's

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:57.000
tax increases would fall on the one percent
on the top one percent.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:03.080
And a lot of that remaining 25 percent would
fall on the top two to four percent.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:04.660
This is serious stuff.

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:07.280
This is serious, radical stuff.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:11.650
The people that then come in and say, well,
he'll never get it done.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:12.650
But hold on.

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:14.289
That that's not just Joe Biden.

00:05:14.289 --> 00:05:18.310
Every president has trouble getting done what
they want to do.

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:22.039
And you would have to apply that exact same
standard, that exact same logic, that exact

00:05:22.039 --> 00:05:23.699
same caveat.

00:05:23.699 --> 00:05:27.810
To Bernie Sanders, you can say, well, it's
not left enough.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:35.639
OK, but say that and recognize that it would
be the most progressive economic policy for

00:05:35.639 --> 00:05:38.349
a sitting president for a long, long time.

00:05:38.349 --> 00:05:42.720
There will be people who come in and say,
but the top marginal tax rate was up in the

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:45.720
90s during Dwight D. Eisenhower presidency.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:46.720
Yes.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.400
But the amount of loopholes available at that
time.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:56.030
And remember, the alternative minimum tax
was not put in place until 1969.

00:05:56.030 --> 00:06:03.710
So prior to that, even with these high sticker
tax rates under Eisenhower, the very rich

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:07.629
were rarely paying anything close to that
because of the amount of loopholes and because

00:06:07.629 --> 00:06:12.039
of the lack of what's called the alternative
minimum tax.

00:06:12.039 --> 00:06:15.680
So you can critique Joe Biden in saying he
doesn't go far enough.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:22.039
For example, Joe Biden wants to reinstate
some of those state and local tax deductions

00:06:22.039 --> 00:06:24.449
that Donald Trump got rid of.

00:06:24.449 --> 00:06:32.480
There is no doubt that there are sort of medium
wealthy and super wealthy people in blue states

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:38.880
that lost some significant deductions when
Trump capped state and local tax deductions.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:44.550
And yes, both the Democratic and Republican
Party are beholden to donors.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:51.750
And that is something Joe Biden wants to reinstate,
but contrasted with the magnitude of the other

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.370
things that he's proposing to do.

00:06:54.370 --> 00:07:01.360
So criticize Joe Biden for not going far enough
contextualized that we have two very corporate

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:05.949
parties that control politics in this country,
do all of that stuff.

00:07:05.949 --> 00:07:13.139
But let's not be blind because of ideology
or laziness or lack of curiosity.

00:07:13.139 --> 00:07:15.720
These are some pretty radical proposals here.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:19.950
And whether or not Joe Biden can get it done,
that's a different question.

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:24.000
Trump hasn't gotten done the things he promised
Bernie would not be able to get done, the

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.920
things he wanted to do.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:29.259
Elizabeth Warren would have had I mean, I
don't know how you pass a wealth tax.

00:07:29.259 --> 00:07:30.319
I really don't.

00:07:30.319 --> 00:07:33.790
But we have to judge by what the platforms
are.

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:35.740
And this is very serious stuff.

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:42.740
In in any case, you are going to have no opportunity
if Donald Trump gets another four years.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:46.940
This is not, you know, the lesser of two evils.

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:48.729
There is clearly a better option here.

00:07:48.729 --> 00:07:50.439
And it is not a small margin.

00:07:50.439 --> 00:07:55.759
It is a dramatic margin between what Donald
Trump wants to do and has done on taxes and

00:07:55.759 --> 00:07:59.660
what Joe Biden, his proposal proposing.

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:51.370
Just 
the facts, my friends.

00:08:51.370 --> 00:09:07.050
Just

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:11.950
the facts.

